# Tests excluded from the sec=krb5p runs only, selected by exclude_file in
# .github/xfstests-variants.json. Same format and the same rules as
# scripts/xfstests-exclude: a test earns a place here only with a reason,
# and only with a reason that is understood.

# generic/486 (a 1-byte to 64 KiB XATTR_REPLACE) fails under krb5p and
# nowhere else. A knfsd decode bug, fixed by
# patches/svcauth-gss-unwrap-priv-krb5p.patch: gss_krb5_unwrap_v2() shortens
# the head iovec by the GSS token header and confounder, but
# svcauth_gss_unwrap_priv() leaves xdr->end pointing past it, so the 64 KiB
# value is consumed 32 bytes out of step where it spans the head and the
# pages. nfsd then reads the next COMPOUND operation from the value and
# returns NFS4ERR_OP_ILLEGAL, which the client reports as EREMOTEIO.
#
# These legs deliberately run the tree as released, so the patch is not
# applied here. xfstests-uml.yml's krb5p-fix jobs run 486 with and without
# it; drop this entry once the fix is upstream and in the tested refs.
generic/486
